+## Updated build for X310 Aurora OOT block
+
 This build is using uhd 4.9.0.1 and the isntructions to build this Aurora image for X310 are as follows:
 
 Build and install UHD from the modified source to get the updated BSP files:                                                                                                                                       
@@ -192,3 +194,20 @@ Build and install UHD from the modified source to get the updated BSP files:
   - build/usrp_x310_fpga_Aurora.bin                                                                                                                                                                                  
   - build/usrp_x310_fpga_Aurora.lvbitx                      
   - build/usrp_x310_fpga_Aurora.rpt
+
+
+Aurora is on SFP+ Port 0 (sfpp0). The AA target's defines are:                                                                                                                                                     
+                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
+  SFP0_RFNOC_AURORA=1   ← aurora on port 0                                                                                                                                                                           
+  SFP1_1GBE=1           ← 1 GigE on port 1                                                                                                                                                                           
+                                                                                                                                                                                                                     
+  On the X310 front panel, SFP0 is the left/top SFP+ cage (the one also used by the 1G/10G Ethernet configurations as the primary port). SFP1 carries the 1 GigE management/data link in this configuration.         
+                                                          
+  The X310's default IP addresses are stored in EEPROM (not in the FPGA bitfile), with factory defaults:                                                                                                             
+  - SFP0 (eth0): 192.168.10.2                                                                                                                                                                                      
+  - SFP1 (eth1): 192.168.20.2                                                                                                                                                                                        
+                             
+  In the X310_AA configuration SFP0 is aurora (bypasses Ethernet entirely), so the 1 GigE interface is on SFP1 at 192.168.20.2. The host NIC should be set to 192.168.20.1/24.                                       
+                                                                                                                                                                                                                     
+  You can verify or change the stored IP with:                                                                                                                                                                       
+  uhd_image_loader --args="type=x300,addr=192.168.20.2" --just-check-rev
